  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse d&apos;urgence en pr&#xe9;vention, prise en charge des Violences Bas&#xe9;es sur le Genre (VBG) et protection contre l&#x2019;exploitation et les abus sexuels dans la province du Nord Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving gender-based violence protection assistance to internally displaced persons, returnees and host community members in Kanya, Karisimbi, Lubero, Masisi, Nyiragongo, and Rutshuru. This UNFPA project procures emergency reproductive health kits, distributes dignity kits, provides conditional cash transfers, supports safe spaces for women and girls, delivers case management services to GBV survivors, reinforces community-based protection mechanisms, and raises awareness about gender-based violence. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 65,300 people, including 15,300 women, 14,500 men, 35,500 children, and including 3,400 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
